# X-13 ARIMA-SEATS binary — download separately from the U.S. Census
# Bureau (own license) per instructions in the User Guide, Section 13.
# See: https://www.census.gov/data/software/x13as.html
resources/x13/

# Working / scratch artifacts (housekeeping). NOTE: gitignore does not untrack
# already-committed files; intentionally-kept output/ files (e.g. byf baselines
# read by tests, phase7 maps) remain on disk but are ignored — `git add -f` to
# version one. Patterns are scoped to avoid clobbering __init__.py / _helpers.
# (.gitignore has no inline comments — keep these on their own lines.)
# output/ = working space; only force-added files are tracked
output/
# harness-managed temp intermediates (regenerated each run)
**/_tmp/
# loose scratch dumps
**/_*.txt
# scratch notes
**/*_scratch*.md

# --- Local-only artifacts (the standing never-stage set) ---
# Run outputs, harness scratch, and session handoff documents: produced
# locally, deliberately never versioned. Ignoring them keeps `git status`
# a signal rather than permanent noise.
bond yield forecast runs/
docs/handoff/
resources/sample_data/CAViaR_Results_*.xlsx
# reports/ is a TRACKED audit-docs directory (90 .md reports). Only the
# underscore-prefixed scratch extensions are ignored, so a future _*.md
# audit report stays committable.
tools/reference_parity/reports/_*.json
tools/reference_parity/reports/_*.err
tools/reference_parity/reports/_*.jsonl
# Build product: regenerated by tools/generate_udf_catalog.ps1 on every
# build_pack run; source of truth is the C# UDF attributes, not this JSON.
# Untracked in the commit that added this line. No CI step reads it;
# tools/smoke_tests.ps1 needs a build_pack (or a direct generator run)
# first on a fresh clone.
resources/catalog/udf_catalog.json
